{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>FLIP has real limits worth knowing</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      FLIP works great for a fixed set of items changing position or size. It's not a general animation library, if you need physics-based motion, gesture-driven dragging, or animating items entering/leaving the list entirely, you'll want a purpose-built library layered on top of the same underlying idea.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Elements need to exist in the DOM at both the First and Last positions for the measurement step to work, items that are newly added or removed during the reorder need separate enter/exit handling, FLIP alone only covers items that persist and move.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      For long lists, batch all First measurements before any DOM mutation happens (avoid interleaving reads and writes, which forces synchronous layout thrashing), then batch all Last measurements after the single DOM update, this is why FLIP implementations measure everything up front rather than element-by-element.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

